' ============================================
' APPLICATION LAYER (Backend - Clean Architecture)
' ============================================
package "APPLICATION Backend API - Clean Architecture (Node.js + Express + TS)" #FFF8E1 {
    
    note as N2
        **Clean Architecture - Onion Model**
        Domain (Core) ← Application ← Infrastructure ← Presentation
        
        **Dependency Rule:**
        • Outer layers depend on inner layers
        • Inner layers know NOTHING about outer layers
        • Abstractions (interfaces) enable Dependency Inversion
        
        **SOLID Principles Applied:**
        • S: Each service has one responsibility
        • O: Services are open for extension via inheritance
        • L: BaseController/BaseService are substitutable
        • I: Small, focused interfaces (no god objects)
        • D: High-level modules depend on abstractions
    end note
    
    ' ============================================
    ' INFRASTRUCTURE LAYER (Framework & Cross-Cutting)
    ' ============================================
    package "INFRASTRUCTURE Infrastructure Layer (Express)" #FFFDE7 {
        component "🚦 Express App\n(HTTP Server)" as ExpressServer #FFE082
        
        package "🛡️ Middleware Pipeline (Cross-Cutting Concerns)" #FFF9C4 {
            component "1️⃣ Helmet\n(Security Headers)" as Helmet #FFD54F
            component "2️⃣ CORS\n(Access Control)" as CORS #FFD54F
            component "3️⃣ Request Logger\n(Correlation ID)" as RequestLogger #FFD54F
            component "4️⃣ Rate Limiter\n(DDoS Protection)" as RateLimiter #FFD54F
            component "5️⃣ Auth Middleware\n(JWT Validation)" as AuthMiddleware #FFD54F
            component "6️⃣ Validation\n(Zod Schemas)" as ValidationMiddleware #FFD54F
            component "7️⃣ Upload Handler\n(Multer)" as UploadMiddleware #FFD54F
            component "⚡ asyncHandler\n(Error Wrapper)" as AsyncHandler #FFD54F
            component "8️⃣ Error Handler\n(Global Catch)" as ErrorHandler #FFD54F
        }
        
        note right of RequestLogger
            **Middleware = Chain of Responsibility Pattern**
            Each middleware decides: pass to next() or terminate
            Cross-cutting concerns isolated from business logic
        end note
        
        note right of AsyncHandler
            **asyncHandler = Higher-Order Function**
            • Wraps ALL async route handlers
            • Eliminates try-catch boilerplate
            • Catches errors → passes to errorHandler
            
            **Before (12 lines):**
            ```typescript
            router.get('/data', async (req, res) => {
              try {
                const data = await service.getData();
                res.json(data);
              } catch (err) {
                next(err);
              }
            });
            ```
            
            **After (4 lines):**
            ```typescript
            router.get('/data', asyncHandler(
              async (req, res) => {
                const data = await service.getData();
                res.json(data);
              }
            ));
            ```
            
            **Impact:**
            • 70+ routes refactored
            • ~600 lines of code eliminated
            • Consistent error handling
            • Impossible to forget error handling
        end note
    }
    
    ' ============================================
    ' PRESENTATION LAYER (API Routes - Thin Layer)
