    | <color:#D32F2F>red dashed</color> | Legacy coupling (⚠️ needs refactoring) |
    
    **🎯 SOLID PRINCIPLES APPLIED:**
    
    **S - Single Responsibility:**
    • Each service has ONE reason to change
    • AgentOrchestrator: orchestration only
    • AIService: AI communication only
    • EmailService: email operations only
    • UserContextService: user data only
    
    **O - Open/Closed:**
    • BaseController: extend for new controllers
    • BaseService<T>: extend for new entities (UserContextService ✅)
    • Middleware: add new without modifying existing
    • Services: open for extension (but not all use inheritance)
    
    **L - Liskov Substitution:**
    • All controllers can replace BaseController ✅
    • UserContextService can replace BaseService<T> ✅
    • Type-safe inheritance (TypeScript generics)
    
    **I - Interface Segregation:**
    • Small, focused interfaces (no god objects)
    • Services expose only needed methods
    • Controllers provide minimal surface area
    • Each service has specific interface
    
    **D - Dependency Inversion:**
    • High-level (AgentOrchestrator) depends on service abstractions
    • Low-level (Supabase, Nodemailer) implements infrastructure
    • BaseService abstracts database operations
    • Services use composition over inheritance when needed
    
    **📐 DESIGN PATTERNS USED:**
    
    **Creational:**
    • Singleton (Logger, Cache, Config)
    • Factory (Error classes, Middleware configurators)
    
    **Structural:**
    • Adapter (AIService wraps Gemini API)
    • Facade (InboxService hides IMAP complexity)
    • Decorator (Middleware wraps request/response)
    • Composite (UI components)
    
    **Behavioral:**
    • Strategy (Cache eviction, Rate limiting)
    • Chain of Responsibility (Middleware pipeline)
    • Observer (Supabase Realtime subscriptions)
    • Mediator/Orchestrator (AgentOrchestrator coordinates services)
    • Template Method (BaseController defines response flow)
    
    **Architectural:**
    • Clean Architecture (Onion Model - 4 layers)
    • Repository Pattern (BaseService<T> - used by UserContextService)
    • Service Layer Pattern (Business logic isolation)
    • Dependency Injection (Services as singletons)
    • CQRS-lite (Read/Write separation in controllers)
    
    **Note on Repository Pattern:**
    Currently only UserContextService uses BaseService<T>.
    Other services use specialized patterns:
    • AIService → API Client pattern
    • EmailService → SMTP Client pattern
    • InboxService → IMAP Client pattern
    • PDFService → Document Generation pattern
    • ScraperService → Web Scraping pattern
    
    **🔄 CLEAN ARCHITECTURE LAYERS:**
    
    **1. Domain (Core) - 💎**
    • Business rules (AgentOrchestrator, AIService, etc.)
    • No dependencies on outer layers
    • Pure TypeScript - no frameworks
    
    **2. Application - 🎯**
    • Use cases (Controllers, Hooks)
    • Orchestrates domain services
    • Depends only on Domain
    
    **3. Infrastructure - 🏗️**
    • Technical details (DB, Logger, Cache, Config)
    • Implements domain interfaces
    • Depends on Domain (Dependency Inversion)
    
    **4. Presentation - 🎨**
    • UI (Pages, Routes)
    • Depends on Application
    • Framework-specific (Next.js, Express)
    
    **📊 ARCHITECTURE QUALITY METRICS:**
    
    ✅ **Testability:** Services isolated, easy to mock
    ✅ **Maintainability:** Clear separation, low coupling
    ✅ **Scalability:** Horizontal scaling ready (stateless)
    ✅ **Security:** RLS, JWT, encryption, rate limiting
    ✅ **Observability:** Structured logging, correlation IDs
    ✅ **Performance:** Caching, connection pooling
    ✅ **Reliability:** Error handling, retry logic
    ✅ **Extensibility:** Open/Closed principle
    
